//@ compile-fail
//@ error-contains: the argument of `assert_throws` can never throw, so this assertion could never pass
//
// `assert_throws(42)` used to be worse than rejected: the checker ignored the assert
// KIND entirely, and lowering turned the assertion into a no-op that silently passed.
// Now the argument is checked with the assertion as its throw sink, and an argument
// that cannot throw is a test that fails on every run — a mistake caught at compile
// time, not on the first execution.

fn main() {
    assert_throws(42);
}
